    {"problem": "The oil tank gauge drops faster than you'd like", "solution": "Oil furnaces in older homes can burn through a fill in one cold stretch. A cold-climate heat pump can take over most of the season, and the oil furnace can stay as backup until you're ready to retire it."},
    {"problem": "Wind off Lake Simcoe chills the lake side of the house", "solution": "Strong shoreline wind pulls heat out of exposed walls. We size from a heat-loss calculation that accounts for that exposure, then add a ductless head where one side of the house lags."},
    {"problem": "A converted cottage runs on a patchwork of heaters", "solution": "Space heaters, a wood stove and a couple of baseboards rarely add up to even heat. A multi-zone ductless system replaces the patchwork with one outdoor unit and a head in each main room, each controlled on its own."},
